# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# 1. The Open Graph images.
#
#    Next's metadata route emits `fr/opengraph-image` — a real 1200x630 PNG with
#    NO file extension. Static hosts derive Content-Type from the extension, so
#    without this rule the file goes out as application/octet-stream and every
#    scraper that fetches it (WhatsApp, Facebook, iMessage, Slack, Twitter)
#    silently drops the preview image. The link still shares; it just shares
#    naked. That matters more than usual here because the site's own demo CTA
#    is a wa.me link, so WhatsApp is the channel the page is most often pasted
#    into.
#
#    Kept as three explicit paths rather than a wildcard: `/*/opengraph-image`
#    would also match any future locale, which is the intent, but Pages matches
#    a bare `*` greedily across slashes and the explicit form is unambiguous.

/fr/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/en/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png
/ar/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/png

# 2. Next's fingerprinted bundles.
#
#    Everything under `_next/static` carries a content hash in its filename, so
#    a given URL's bytes never change. Year-long immutable caching is the
#    contract that filename is making; without it the CDN revalidates 2 MB of
#    unchanged JavaScript on every visit.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# 3. The app's own assets.
#
#    Sans règle, Cloudflare Pages sert `/assets/*` en
#    `max-age=14400, must-revalidate`. Passé quatre heures, `must-revalidate`
#    interdit au navigateur de réutiliser un fichier sans avoir redemandé au
#    serveur — soit ~130 allers-retours bloquants avant que le tableau de bord
#    démarre, plusieurs fois par jour, pour des octets qui n'ont pas bougé.
#
#    Pas d'`immutable` ici, contrairement à `_next/static` : 63 des fichiers
#    que charge `dashboard.html` n'ont PAS d'estampille `?v=` (`auth-guard.js`,
#    `kiwi-env.js`, `theme.css`…). Les figer un an, c'est se priver du moyen de
#    corriger un bug d'authentification chez un client déjà venu.
#
#    `stale-while-revalidate` donne les deux : la copie en cache part
#    immédiatement, sans attendre le réseau, et la mise à jour se fait derrière.
#    Une estampille qui bouge reste servie tout de suite, puisque l'URL change.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800
